        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[[url] Using URLSearchParams.delete method changes the enconding of unrelated search params]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34896</link>
            <guid>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34896</guid>
            <pubDate>Wed, 17 Jul 2024 13:22:45 GMT</pubDate>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3 dir="auto">What type of issue is this?</h3>
<p dir="auto">Browser bug (a bug with a feature that may impact site compatibility)</p>
<h3 dir="auto">What information was incorrect, unhelpful, or incomplete?</h3>
<p dir="auto">There should be a warning about the lack of consistency of the method while working with URI Encoded Search Params.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">What browsers does this problem apply to, if applicable?</h3>
<p dir="auto">Chromium (Chrome, Edge 79+, Opera, Samsung Internet), Firefox</p>
<h3 dir="auto">What did you expect to see?</h3>
<p dir="auto">A section with a example involving the usage of a Encoded URI search param. Such as:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="const url = new URL(&quot;https://example.com?search=1234&amp;param=my%20param&quot;);
console.log(`Query string (before):\t ${url.search}`);
url.searchParams.delete(&quot;search&quot;);
console.log(`Query string (after):\t ${url.search}`); "><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-k">const</span> <span class="pl-s1">url</span> <span class="pl-c1">=</span> <span class="pl-k">new</span> <span class="pl-c1">URL</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">"https://example.com?search=1234&amp;param=my%20param"</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">`Query string (before):\t <span class="pl-s1"><span class="pl-kos">${</span><span class="pl-s1">url</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">search</span><span class="pl-kos">}</span></span>`</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-s1">url</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">searchParams</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">delete</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">"search"</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span>
<span class="pl-smi">console</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-en">log</span><span class="pl-kos">(</span><span class="pl-s">`Query string (after):\t <span class="pl-s1"><span class="pl-kos">${</span><span class="pl-s1">url</span><span class="pl-kos">.</span><span class="pl-c1">search</span><span class="pl-kos">}</span></span>`</span><span class="pl-kos">)</span><span class="pl-kos">;</span> </pre></div>
<h3 dir="auto">Did you test this? If so, how?</h3>
<p dir="auto">You can simply paste it on Firefox/Chromium console and get this output:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="Query string (before):	 ?search=1234&amp;param=my%20param
Query string (after):	 ?param=my+param"><pre class="notranslate"><code class="notranslate">Query string (before):	 ?search=1234&amp;param=my%20param
Query string (after):	 ?param=my+param
</code></pre></div>
<h3 dir="auto">Can you link to any release notes, bugs, pull requests, or MDN pages related to this?</h3>
<p dir="auto">Couldn't find any</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Do you have anything more you want to share?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
<h3 dir="auto">MDN URL</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/URLSearchParams/delete" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/URLSearchParams/delete</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">MDN metadata</h3>

<details>
<summary>MDN page report details</summary>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Query: <code class="notranslate">api.URLSearchParams.delete</code></li>
<li>Report started: 2024-07-17T13:07:48.355Z</li>
</ul>
</details>]]></content:encoded>
